18980a89-5d63-4773-bd8e-441008b8ddc4"},"useSeparator":"auto"},{"content":{"params":{"overallFeedback":[{"from":0,"to":100}],"behaviour":{"autoContinue":true,"timeoutCorrect":2000,"timeoutWrong":3000,"soundEffectsEnabled":true,"enableRetry":false,"enableSolutionsButton":false,"passPercentage":100},"l10n":{"nextButtonLabel":"Next question","showSolutionButtonLabel":"Show solution","retryButtonLabel":"Retry","solutionViewTitle":"Solution list","correctText":"Correct!","incorrectText":"Incorrect!","shouldSelect":"Should have been selected","shouldNotSelect":"Should not have been selected","muteButtonLabel":"Mute feedback sound","closeButtonLabel":"Close","slideOfTotal":"Slide :num of :total","scoreBarLabel":"You got :num out of :total points","solutionListQuestionNumber":"Question :num","a11yShowSolution":"Show the solution. The task will be marked with its correct solution.","a11yRetry":"Retry the task. Reset all responses and start the task over again."},"choices":[{"subContentId":"ccf67daa-845c-4fa0-a290-d475b465070d","question":"<p>1. What is the main purpose of the video?</p>","answers":["<p>To explain what a carbon footprint is and how it can be reduced</p>","<p>To tell a story about climate change</p>","<p>To describe animals in the world</p>","<p>To compare different countries only</p>"]},{"subContentId":"1e1b4d21-bd7a-4c7b-a720-05602d1ed61e","question":"<p>2. What does the term <em>carbon footprint</em> mean?</p>","answers":["<p>The total amount of greenhouse gases produced by activities</p>","<p>The amount of heat on the earth</p>","<p>The number of cars in the world</p>","<p>The temperature of the planet</p>"]},{"subContentId":"9121c206-9bed-48f6-adc8-45101a4e93db","question":"<p>3. Which activity gives a direct impact on carbon footprint?</p>","answers":["<p>Traveling using cars</p>","<p>Reading books</p>","<p>Sleeping</p>","<p>Watching TV without electricity</p>"]},{"subContentId":"f305385e-b2a2-46ad-8dfb-8d0bd22d521d","question":"<p>4. According to the video, which is one effective way to reduce carbon footprint?</p>","answers":["<p>Using sustainable energy</p>","<p>Using more plastic</p>","<p>Taking more flights</p>","<p>Driving more cars</p>"]},{"subContentId":"c591339f-3068-4157-98e4-925e23b77913","question":"<p>5. Which statement is a FACT from the video?</p>","answers":["<p>Transport is a big part of carbon footprint</p>","<p>Reducing carbon footprint is impossible</p>","<p>People should stop using electricity</p>","<p>All countries produce the same emissions</p>"]},{"subContentId":"38a8d5b5-67d2-4e73-a498-613a387bcaa8","question":"<p>6. Which statement is an OPINION from the video?</p>","answers":["<p>People in richer countries need to make huge changes</p>","<p>Greenhouse gases trap heat in the atmosphere</p>","<p>The UK produces about 5.5 tonnes per person</p>","<p>Methane is a greenhouse gas</p>"]},{"subContentId":"34818134-3160-4eed-8a5f-ffb85a1856f7","question":"<p>7. Why does eating red meat increase carbon footprint?</p>","answers":["<p>Because cows produce methane gas</p>","<p>Because meat needs electricity</p>","<p>Because people cook too much</p>","<p>Because food is expensive</p>"]},{"subContentId":"261c25b9-315e-4e36-b187-53123ced8405","question":"<p>8. What can be inferred about richer countries?</p>","answers":["<p>They consume more goods and energy</p>","<p>They produce less pollution</p>","<p>They do not use technology</p>","<p>They have no carbon footprint</p>"]},{"subContentId":"f9811612-83bb-435c-bd42-649f35241348","question":"<p>9. Which sentence shows modality used in the video?</p>","answers":["<p>You should probably reduce it</p>","<p>Carbon footprint refers to greenhouse gases</p>","<p>Transport is a big part of carbon footprints</p>","<p>Methane is a greenhouse gas</p>"]},{"subContentId":"8200123b-74e1-4576-aeb0-dc5f5aaddcb1","question":"<p>10. What is the recommendation of the video?</p>","answers":["<p>People must change their lifestyle to reduce emissions</p>","<p>Carbon footprint ca